# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
"""Colour by number on paintings, made for an older player.

A picture is split into regions, each with a number; the palette at the
bottom has one big button per number. Pick a colour, tap its regions.
- Regions still to paint are grey, lighter or darker as the colour they
  wait for; those of the chosen number are light blue with their number
  bold, so they are easy to find. A region of another number cannot be
  painted.
- A tap a little beside a region of the chosen number still paints it:
  a finger is wider than the smallest regions.
- Numbers show once they are large enough to read; small regions show
  theirs when zoomed in.
- The buttons on the right carry drawn icons, no words: zoom in, zoom
  out (down to the whole picture on screen), "whole picture" (one tap
  fits the picture to the screen, the next one goes back to the same
  zoom and place), "where?" (puts the nearest unpainted region of the
  chosen colour in the middle, zoomed in until its number reads), undo,
  and "look" (the finished picture while held). A drag moves the
  picture, which glides on when let go; a zoom takes a moment's glide.
  Two fingers zoom it, about where they met, where the desktop passes
  them; moving it is for one finger.
  Fingers are followed one by one (GTK's gestures follow only the
  first): a finger that does not move taps, unless another one was on
  the screen just then; one lying still for a while (a thumb holding
  the tablet, or one whose lift was lost after a palm) is left out.
- A wrong tap gets a red outline; there is no timer, no score, no ads.
- Progress is saved after every tap, so a picture can wait for tomorrow;
  the program starts on the last picture, unless it is finished, and the
  gallery opens at that picture's card. A finished picture shows
  without its outlines and numbers, and "Сохранить в галерею" keeps it
  as a PNG in Изображения/Мои раскраски, where Галерея shows it.

Pictures are gzipped SVG made by pbn.py: one path per region, with its
number and the point where the number goes. The gallery has paintings
of about 120, 300 and 600 regions, and a section of Japanese prints. To
stay quick on a slow tablet (no GPU: a full redraw takes a second), the
picture is drawn in tiles at the current zoom by a thread of its own and
kept until the zoom changes; a drag only copies tiles, a zoom stretches
what is there until the new tiles come, a tap paints its region into the
tiles kept. Progress is written a moment after the last tap, and gallery
thumbnails are kept as PNG files.

It is a GTK application, io.github.haltia_de.Paint (io.github.trudenboy.Paint
before 4.0), for any desktop; on the Haltia tablet shell the shell buzzes
the touches and its GTK theme gives the large header and dialogs. Its
folders were called b8k-paint before 4.0 and move on the first start.

Pictures: the built-in ones in PREFIX/share/haltia-paint/, and any photo
put into ~/Раскраски (JPEG or PNG), which is turned into a picture of
about 300 regions in the background the first time the gallery sees it.

The gallery is built once and kept: closing a picture redraws only its
card; the first screenful shows at once and the other cards come while
it is already in use, their thumbnails drawn in a thread.

New pictures: "+ Добавить" in the gallery header offers a picture from
the tablet's own (the pictures, downloads and camera folders and memory
cards, newest first, as Галерея finds them) or a search: it searches
Wikidata for
paintings (items that are an instance of painting and have an image), by
artist, title or what is painted, in Russian as well; the pictures
themselves come from Wikimedia Commons, where every file is under a free
licence and most paintings are in the public domain. A tap on a result
shows it large with its artist and year, as it will look painted at the
chosen size of regions (a tap on it shows the painting itself). pbn.py
makes it in a process of its own at low priority, as it takes 15 to 30
seconds on the tablet. "Загрузить" keeps it in
~/.local/share/haltia-paint/downloaded/, shown in its own gallery section,
where "✕ Убрать" takes it out again. Only https requests to
wikidata.org, commons.wikimedia.org and the Wikimedia image hosts are
made.
"""
